    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="1005" n="891" xml:id="pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">374.115 Standard Oil Company/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shoemaker</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-30T18:00:00+02:00">November 30, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 30—4:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>33. Referring Department’s telegram No. 10, November 27. Legation made
                    representations only upon verifying costs from company, which was selling at
                    Commission’s price, or lower, for reasons of business competition. An
                    examination of another company’s books by an agent of the Commission within the
                    last month revealed loss of 1½ leva per kilo.</p>
                <p>As requested, Legation is mailing comprehensive statement of material factors to
                    Department by pouch today<anchor n="3" xml:id="d758-f1"/> and will request
                    Department’s advice should further representations seem necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shoemaker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
